From 6cea1530a5794b9868b53a7762d57c2046423d4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 23:02:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server : device-resident context checkpoint ring + tool-call
 anchor (R31 P1/P2, FreeToken M14/M15)

Context checkpoints on the GDN hybrids (the seat) are host copies of the
recurrent state, ~0.9 s per prompt (SPINE section 6), which is why the seat
runs --ctx-checkpoints 0 and re-prefills every agent turn. Upstream already
has an on-device state path (LLAMA_STATE_SEQ_FLAGS_ON_DEVICE), but one copy
per sequence: a second get overwrites the first, so a ring of checkpoints
could not use it.

llama.h / llama-context: LLAMA_STATE_SEQ_FLAGS_STORAGE(i) (flag bits 8..15)
selects a device storage slot; mem_storage is keyed by (storage, seq_id) so
up to 256 on-device copies per sequence coexist. Storage 0 keeps the old
behaviour byte-for-byte (spec checkpoints, test-save-load-state).

common: common_prompt_checkpoint remembers the flags it was captured with
(flags_tgt/flags_dft) and an anchor bit; on_device() tells the prompt
cache which checkpoints cannot survive a RAM round trip.

server: --ctx-checkpoints-device auto|on|off (auto = on for recurrent/hybrid
targets, off = the host copy = generic path); each checkpoint takes a
round-robin storage id from a ring of n_ctx_checkpoints+1, so a reused id is
always dead. Restore uses the captured flags. The RAM prompt cache keeps only
host-resident checkpoints. --ctx-checkpoints-toolcall on|off: the first
sampled tool-call opener (chat-template grammar trigger token, or
LLAMA_TOOLCALL_ANCHOR_TOKEN) freezes an anchor checkpoint right before the
opener is decoded, exempt from min-step thinning, so a client that rewrites
the echoed tool call still resumes at the anchor.

tests: test-save-load-state Test 9 (device storage ring) - RED on the
single-store code, GREEN with the ring.

Not measured in this commit (POOL MODE, non-measuring lane): the served A/B
(ckpt 0 vs host 32 vs device 32 on the 20-turn agent transcript) is the serial
lane's, see HANDOFF-TO-SERIAL.md in the R31 report folder.

Origin: FreeToken (FlashML-org, af71ba43) hybrid_radix_cache.py:76-113, linear_state_pool.py:188-194, scheduler.py:117-125 / :357-362 / :866-871 (tool-call anchor); upstream on-device state path d6e7b033a; port by ArifiLabs lane-223 R31 (Fable 5.1 MEDIUM, kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - correctness test staged (test-save-load-state Test 9); served A/B owed to the serial lane
Lane: lane-223
(cherry picked from commit cdff32828b30411c3beeb75ab70be89bdc62a8e7)
